  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Mechanism
    
    Shawl☽ Sun is a fire-memory magic that operates by controlled inversion: rather than drawing heat from the Berg's volcanic core, the practitioner ignites the ice itself, forcing it to release the impressions frozen within. A hairline fracture appears in the surface first, followed by warmth described consistently across sources as tasting of copper and ash. The practitioner then perceives what the ice recorded — events years or centuries old, preserved as ghost-scenes in the deep layers. At this point a choice presents itself: witness only, or burn the memory away entirely, leaving unmarked ice behind.
    
    Forge-grade fire-cores, traded by the ☽'ofund' Guild (a Nightshelf merchant guild based at Wane☽ Oncea), are among the materials employed in Shawl☽ Sun work, though the practice's essential catalyst is not fire-core heat but the resonance of **The Dreaming Tooth**, an orca artifact of enormous antiquity currently held by the Wake-Singers at the Corpse Current.
    
    ## Discovery and Cost
    
    The summary record attributes the discovery to ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~, a Nightshelf outlaw, near Thrall☽ Vavmastius. The archive's earliest account specifies that she pressed the Dreaming Tooth against corrupted ice at Terrace Momiou and watched the corruption unravel into visions. Whether these refer to the same incident at adjacent sites or to separate events is unresolved.
    
    The cost is cumulative and irreversible. Each use thins the practitioner's own memories. ☽'Retenusus the Undimmed, Dominus — a master at the underground colony of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ — forgot his own name within a season of learning the practice. The chronicle *The City that Grew Fat on Fire* records that Retenusus and his followers continued burning deeper into the tunnels despite three warnings from the ice, ultimately triggering a catastrophic structural failure that released superheated steam and killed — the chronicle claims — a thousand penguins. I note the round number.
    
    ## Practitioners and Legacy
    
    Those who followed ☽'Saetacaeia-Viamana~'s method called themselves the **Sun-Shawled**, an informal alliance that gathered at corruption sites across the Nightshelf to burn ice clean and sell the blank stone to merchants. The practitioner list is longer than the fables suggest; the relationships on file name at least nine, including Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ (founder of ☽'slew Nisaemesius~) and ☽'tenebris, called the Hollow Dealer in fable tradition — a merchant who dealt in memory-burned ice until, the fables hold, she could not remember the name of her own colony.
    
    Nightshelf fable tradition classifies Shawl☽ Sun as *the gift with teeth*: the bargain that sounds fair but devours the bargainer. The moral attributed to ☽'tenebris is plain — **you may take the secret or the self, but not both**.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
